      en: "Plover Cove Reservoir is Hong Kong's largest reservoir with a capacity of 230 million cubic meters. It was completed in 1968 by building a 1.9 km long dam across Tolo Harbour. The reservoir has a water surface area of 12.4 km² and is located in Plover Cove Country Park. The dam is one of the longest sea-water dams in Asia at 25 m high. The reservoir supplies about 25% of Hong Kong's drinking water. The surrounding hills offer hiking trails and birdwatching, including the endangered black-faced spoonbill.",
